-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Prince of the Yolkfolk
  Publisher   Code Masters, 1991
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dizzy 6 - Dizzy, Prince of the YolkFolk (1991)(Code
              Masters)(128K)[a][a][aka Dizzy VI - Prince of the Yolkfolk].z80
  MD5         292c1b1ca9f78dac32045533c9ba5361

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the plain
              .nex as control, input keyed to the game loop update 0x786E,
              lockstep checked at every update (equal in all 30 trials), SPACE
              tapped in boxes and the title by the game's own input poll)

  Changes     1.0: Dean Woodyatt's Prince of the Yolkfolk build moved to the
              128K release (AY music), his plot hook at 28 MHz, whole alt ROM
              image with the mirrored Dizzy's plotter, loading screen

  Note        The 128K release, so the AY music plays. Dean Woodyatt's Prince
              of the Yolkfolk build: Dizzy is four hardware sprites, so he no
              longer takes the colours of the scenery he walks through; the
              mirrored Dizzy in Double Trouble stays on the screen as in the
              original. His plot hook now runs at 28 MHz. Loading screen from
              the tape. Known issues: where the original's eraser leaves a
              small hole in an object drawn over Dizzy, this build keeps it
              whole (5 of 171,382 pixel checks). Missing: no Enhanced colour
              set (rated easy); the archive's Animation speed and second
              Infinite lives cheats (one asks for a value, the other stops the
              game); only the start rooms and Double Trouble checked in
              testing; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Immune to bats
   3  Immune to flame of torch
   4  Immune to flames of burnt
   5  Immune to troll
   6  Immune to ferryman
   7  Extra energy
   8  Start with 20 cherries

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

