-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      5 recordings of the 128K release on rework v128 (bot walks: two
              of 6,013 / 6,330 frames in Double Trouble, the mirrored Dizzy's
              room, reached with the game's own room skip, and three of 12,008
              / 12,015 / 12,163 frames from the start): every hook event
              identical: 8,182 player plots (8,779 sprite pictures pixel-
              perfect), 8,686 erases, 18,603 ISR checks, 130 room wipes and 90
              boxes hiding Dizzy, 1,022 mirrored-Dizzy plots and 989 erases
              equal to the original's; 3 recordings IDENTICAL; 2 differ in 5
              of 171,382 pixel tests, where the original's eraser leaves a
              hole or a ghost pixel in an object drawn over Dizzy (the build
              keeps the object whole); 8 negative controls detected; clock
              matrix 7 hook sites x 4 incoming clocks = 28 cases PASS, a
              forced 3.5 MHz exit detected; ROM paths: every ROM byte as
              recorded; start-up tail never read before written; R never read

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: loading screen, title, play reached,
              frames viewed; AY music written (700 data writes a second in
              play, as the original); flicker 300 frames: 0 out of step, 0
              vanished, 0 transients; 15-minute soak against the original
              .z80: no freeze or crash, one loop warning on the game's own
              4-frame wait with Dizzy moving (frames viewed); no person played
              it

  Coverage    the start rooms, the title and Double Trouble (the mirrored
              Dizzy) only (bot walks); loading screen stub in bank 13,
              emulator-tested only; cheats proved in the simulator on the 128K
              file: Infinite Lives: lives stayed 3 after a death (2 without);
              Immune to Bats, Flame of Torch, Flames of Burnt Door, Troll,
              Ferryman: each hazard's damage call run from a play state left
              the energy at 31 (29, 30, 0, 23, 23 without); Extra energy: 62
              at the start (31); Start with 20 cherries: 20 (0); dropped:
              Animation speed (asks the player for a value, which a patch
              cannot hold) and the second Infinite lives (made for another
              layout: it overwrites the 128K release's AY paging routine and
              the game stops)

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
